WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:16.470 align:start position:0%
 
uh  how often have i heard that eisen onion  iron union that's what the fans chant  for their club here in east berlin  let me tell you it's not an ordinary  club  i used to play in the stadium  okay at that time there were fewer  spectators  but the atmosphere was always amazing  i'm pascal i'm a former onion player and  today a sports reporter for kickoff  i want to explain what makes onyon so  special and when my time here came to an  end  for me it all started 10 years ago on  this piece of artificial turf my first  training session since then a lot of  things have changed  for example this gymnasium behind me  didn't exist  but there's one thing that hasn't  changed  in all sorts of colors things were  different then  things have developed it wasn't always  easy for you players  a lot of you came from work and some had  to go to school i still remember that  and the changing rooms were always a  mess  the changing rooms zoozy's domain  she's been working at onion for 20 years  she deals with all the everyday concerns  the youngsters face  and makes sure they get the clothes they  need  susie is the heart of the club  because i helped a lot with the building  up of the youth system this became my  life  that's the only way to put it  nowadays it really is my life and i like  it i like to be with the youngsters i  like being here  and you're someone they can talk to the  second mom  yes and there are players who say hey  mom how are you so we have that too and  it amuses us a bit  but i do think they kind of like me  susie even did my laundry for three  years i took to the pitch as a defender  for onion going up against bundesliga  players to be like kevin and jerome  boateng  but they are the exceptions  just a couple of players from a  bundesliga used team gopro one or two a  year  i lacked the necessary drive the  absolute will to do it my studies were  more important to me and so i left union  behind  of course the fans can't imagine life  without onyon on matchdays they meet up  here at the local bar right next to the  stadium  the place is also a little museum  the walls are covered in history  refounded in east germany in 1966  underdogs on yeon always had to fight  for survival  they were always an anti-establishment  club  and drew in freethinkers to their fan  base  their arch enemy was bfc dynamo berlin  the favorite club of the stasi the east  german secret police  it's a fierce rivalry to this day  andrea's witnessed it all he's been an  unknown fan as long as he can remember  he even saw me play  andreas knows this club better than  anyone  meinhardt ins calacon  hedmut kyle  wolfgang hillman for the co-trainer here  young stop he is walking on your  dictionary  you've been coming for 40 years what's  so fascinating about this club  what's fascinating is it's always been  the same theme munon never really played  successful football but you had 90  minutes of power in the house there was  constant chanting of eisenhunyon it got  to the opponents we definitely didn't  always have the best players but our  team spirit was extreme  extreme  bonyon fans stick together  during christmas season they even meet  up in the stadium to sing christmas  carols  no football necessary  and when it comes to their stadium they  are not afraid to get their hands dirty  the rundown alte first array was  renovated entirely by the fans  they volunteered their services as well  as painters and diggers to save the club  some money and then by the thousands  they even bought shares of their new  stadium  it was a feeling of togetherness the  baker from kaepernick brought the rules  the ice cream man came by there'd never  be that kind of togetherness anywhere  else every club ought to go through that  for a year every day there were 30 or 40  construction workers there it wasn't  easy sometimes it was 20 degrees and  sometimes 20 below  i think that's unique at least in europe  or maybe even in the football world  fans are very proud of it just like  today every bundesliga stadium changes  its name every two or three years the  out to first july will still be the out  to first arrive 30 years from now and  we're proud of that hardly any club can  claim that  things are different at onyon  i noticed that right away back in the  day  they cheer for the players even after a  boring scoreless draw  the relationship between the fans and  the team is an especially close one here  but i'm not a part of that anymore or  onyon is no longer a part of me  why is that  is it my profession my journalistic  distance  at the end of the day i'm no longer a  fan  i'm a critical observer of this  overhyped business of football  the club has now established itself in  the bundesliga second division  i'm not the only one who's changed  as well  i remember sebastian brunich from the  old days when he was a fans favorite and  a hero of the club's promotion  today he is an assistant coach here  and on is a matter of the heart for him  i've got a one-year-old brother who also  played football at some clubs in the  west  i witnessed often enough that they were  booed out of the stadium and insulted  after playing badly  i hardly ever experienced that here here  sometimes we had a lot of really bad  games  sometimes so bad you couldn't watch them  the people here always stand by the club  and the team  that is really exceptional and it's  still like that now  identification is a big word you have to  live it you have to feel it  every person who works for the team  sacrifices him or herself for the work  and the players have to do that too  of course it's professional football  nowadays players come and go but we're  trying to keep the youth here grounded  so that they appreciate what they have  here  i also appreciated my time at unyon and  always gave my all as a player  in the end i chose a different path  but they stayed here sebastian brunich  and fans like andreas  and the carer susie  it's the people who make onyon so  likeable  a club which is a part of my history  and one which you don't forget so easily  that's why it's aizan onyon  iron union

